    "type": "Sensor",
    "description": "The Omron E3FA-DP12 is a compact, cylindrical diffuse-reflective photoelectric sensor designed for reliable object detection in industrial automation systems.\n🔹 Detailed Description\nThe E3FA-DP12 is part of Omron's E3FA series and is built for non-contact detection of objects using reflected light. It emits a red LED beam, and when an object enters the sensing area, the reflected light is detected and the sensor switches its output. \nIt is widely used in continuous industrial processes, where accurate and fast detection is required, such as conveyors, packaging, and assembly lines. \n🔹 Construction &amp; Design\n\n\nShape: Cylindrical (M18 threaded body)\n\n\nHousing material: Durable ABS plastic\n\n\nCompact size: Easy mounting in tight spaces\n\n\nCable type: Pre-wired (typically 2 m cable) \n\n\nThe rugged design provides high resistance to dust, water, and washdown conditions with IP67/IP69K protection. \n🔹 Working Principle\n\n\nUses diffuse reflection method\n\n\nSensor emits light &rarr; object reflects light &rarr; receiver detects it\n\n\nOutput changes based on detection (presence/absence of object)\n\n\n🔹 Key Technical Description\n\n\nSensing distance: Up to 300 mm (depending on target)\n\n\nLight source: Red LED (~624 nm) \n\n\nOutput type: PNP (open collector)\n\n\nOperation modes: Light-ON / Dark-ON selectable\n\n\nSupply voltage: 10&ndash;30 V DC\n\n\nResponse time: ~0.5 ms (high-speed detection) \n\n\n🔹 Functional Features\n\n\nAdjustable sensitivity (single-turn potentiometer)\n\n\nVisible LED indicators for operation and stability\n\n\nProtection circuits:\n\n\nReverse polarity protection\n\n\nShort-circuit protection\n\n\n\n\nStable detection even in harsh industrial environments \n\n\n🔹 Typical Applications\n\n\nConveyor object detection\n\n\nBottle/carton detection\n\n\nPackaging machines\n\n\nAssembly automation\n\n\nFood &amp; beverage industries\n\n\n🔹 Summary\nThe E3FA-DP12 is a reliable, compact, and easy-to-install photoelectric sensor that offers stable short-range detection (up to 300 mm) with high durability, making it ideal for industrial automation and high-speed production lines.",
