    "type": "Sensor",
    "description": "📘 E3FA-RP22 Description\nThe Omron E3FA-RP22 is a cylindrical retro-reflective photoelectric sensor from Omron Corporation, designed for precise and reliable object detection in industrial automation systems.\n🔍 Detailed Description\nThe E3FA-RP22 works on a coaxial retro-reflective sensing principle with an MSR (Mirror Surface Rejection) function, which allows it to detect objects accurately even in the presence of shiny or reflective surfaces. It emits a red LED light beam (around 624 nm) toward a reflector, and detection occurs when the beam is interrupted or altered by an object. (Omron)\nThis sensor has a sensing range of up to 500 mm (when used with a suitable reflector like E39-R1S), making it suitable for short to medium-distance detection tasks. (Omron)\n⚙️ Functional Characteristics\n\n\nSensing type: Retro-reflective (with reflector)\n\n\nLight source: Red LED\n\n\nOutput: PNP open collector\n\n\nSupply voltage: 10&ndash;30 VDC\n\n\nResponse time: Approx. 0.5 ms (fast switching)\n\n\nOperation modes: Light-ON / Dark-ON selectable\n\n\nConnection: M12 connector (4-pin)\n\n\nHousing: M18 cylindrical body\n\n\nProtection: IP67 / IP69K (waterproof &amp; dustproof) (Omron)\n\n\n🏭 Usage Description (Where it is used)\nThe sensor is widely used in:\n\n\nConveyor belt systems for object detection\n\n\nPackaging and bottling machines\n\n\nMaterial handling and counting systems\n\n\nAutomation lines and assembly machines\n\n\nIt provides non-contact detection, improving system reliability and reducing wear compared to mechanical switches. (IndMALL Automation)\n👍 Key Advantages\n\n\nStable detection even for shiny or transparent objects (MSR function)\n\n\nFast response suitable for high-speed automation\n\n\nCompact and rugged design for industrial environments\n\n\nEasy installation with standard M12 connector\n\n\nHigh resistance to dust, water, and vibration\n\n\n📌 Summary\nThe E3FA-RP22 is a reliable, compact, and high-performance photoelectric sensor ideal for industrial automation. Its retro-reflective design with MSR technology ensures accurate detection, even in challenging conditions, making it a popular choice in modern manufacturing systems.\nIf you want, I can also give:\n\n\nWiring diagram 🔌\n\n\nExact switching output explanation\n\n\nComparison with E3FA-RP11 / DP22 / DP13 models",
